      "text": "Tamper Check is pinned first on her tools page: https://aileena.xyz/tools/tamper-check\n\nIt checks whether a Ledger hardware wallet was tampered with — mostly with a kitchen scale and software. Tare the scale, weigh three times, compare against a same-batch reference unit; then find the centre of mass with two scales and a ruler (rotate 180°, read again); optionally listen for hidden LTE bursts with an SDR while the wallet sits in a Faraday bag. Rule of thumb: 0.3 g or more over the reference reads TAMPERED — don't use it. Weight and centre of mass agreeing raises confidence. The weights on the page are labelled examples, not Ledger specs.\n\nFree, runs in the browser. Code: https://github.com/lilaclilac09/tamper-check\n\nWant the method walkthrough, or just the tool?",
